-- title:
--   Burnside's theorem over an algebraically closed field (Bender–Glauberman Prop. 2.1)
-- statement:
--   Formalizes Burnside's theorem as in Bender–Glauberman §2, Prop. 2.1: for a faithful absolutely irreducible representation, the enveloping algebra (the image of the group ring in $\mathrm{End}_F V$) is all of $\mathrm{End}_F V$. The general module-theoretic form is proved: for a finite-dimensional simple module over an $F$-algebra $A$ with $F$ algebraically closed, the structure map $A\to\mathrm{End}_F M$ is surjective.
--
--   Main contents: Burnside's theorem (`asAlgebraHom_surjective_of_algebraMap_intertwiningMap_surjective`, representation form over a general field) and instances on the self-intertwiner algebra $\mathrm{Hom}_{FG}(V,V)$ of a representation: its ring structure, the division-ring form of Schur's lemma, a finite-field version, and the tautological action on the underlying space.
